reserving side's table, thus allowing the OUTER JOIN to be converted to an INNER JOIN for efficiency.\n**Transformations**: Convert OUTER JOINS to INNER JOINS when followed by WHERE clauses that eliminate the possibility of NULL results from the non-preserving side. For example, `SELECT * FROM A LEFT OUTER JOIN B ON condition1 WHERE B.column IS NOT NULL` can be efficiently rewritten as `SELECT * FROM A INNER JOIN B ON condition1` because the WHERE clause enforces a logic that requires a match in B for every row returned.\n```\n\nLogical Plan Changes After Rewrite: ```\n  LogicalSort(sort0=[$0(i_item_id)], sort1=[$1(s_state)], dir0=[ASC], dir1=[ASC], fetch=[100])\n    LogicalAggregate(group=[{0, 1}], groups=[[{0, 1}, {0}, {}]], g_state=[GROUPING($1)], agg1=[AVG($2)], agg2=[AVG($3)], agg3=[AVG($4)], agg4=[AVG($5)])\n      LogicalProject(i_item_id=[$90(i_item_id)], s_state=[$84(s_state)], ss_quantity=[$10(ss_quantity)], ss_list_price=[$12(ss_list_price)], ss_coupon_amt=[$19(ss_coupon_amt)], ss_sales_price=[$13(ss_sales_price)])\n-       LogicalFilter(condition=[AND(=($0(ss_sold_date_sk), $32(d_date_sk)), =($2(ss_item_sk), $89(i_item_sk)), =($7(ss_store_sk), $60(s_store_sk)), =($4(ss_cdemo_sk), $23(cd_demo_sk)), =(CAST($24(cd_gender)):CHAR(1), 'F'), =(CAST($25(cd_marital_status)):CHAR(1), 'S'), =(CAST($26(cd_education_status)):CHAR(7), 'Unknown'), =($38(d_year), 2001), =(CAST($84(s_state)):CHAR(2), 'MI'), =(CAST($101(i_category)):CHAR(5), 'Books'))])\n+       LogicalJoin(condition=[=($2(ss_item_sk), $89(i_item_sk))], joinType=[inner])\n-         LogicalJoin(condition=[true], joinType=[inner])\n?                                  -\n\n+         LogicalJoin(condition=[=($7(ss_store_sk), $60(s_store_sk))], joinType=[inner])\n?                                +++++++++ +  ++++++++++++++++++++++\n\n-           LogicalJoin(condition=[true], joinType=[inner])\n+           LogicalJoin(condition=[=($0(ss_sold_date_sk), $32(d_date_sk))], joinType=[inner])\n-             LogicalJoin