lumn3,\n        SUM(column2) AS total_column2\n    FROM \n        table2\n    GROUP BY \n        column3\n) t2\nLEFT JOIN \n    table1 t1 ON t1.column4 = t2.column3\nGROUP BY \n    t1.column1;\n```\n\nFinally, we can apply `AGGREGATE_REMOVE`. Since the query includes a GROUP BY clause with aggregate functions and each aggregate function is splittable (SUM), we can remove the GROUP BY clause.\n\nThe transformed query would be:\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n    column3,\n    SUM(column2) AS total_column2\nFROM \n    table2\nGROUP BY \n    column3;\n```\n\nThis query can then be used as a subquery in the original query, replacing the scalar subquery.', 'time': 4.650343894958496}
